(thermos, ½l capacity each) 2
(thermometer)
(oven, or any other place without air flow)
(fridge)

::instructions

(milk) <heat, to 45°C / 113°F>
{yogurt mixture} = (milk) + (yogurt)
{yogurt mixture} <whisk>
{yogurt mixture} <heat, to 45°C / 113°F; do not go higher>
(water, for washing thermos) <boil>
(thermos) <wash, inside, with (water, for washing thermos)>
(thermos) <empty>
{yogurt mixture} <pour, into (thermos)>
(thermos) <leave, in (oven, or any other place without air flow), 12h>
(thermos) <store, in (fridge)>

::source
<<<
---
title: "Yogurt"
date: 2021-03-12
tags: ['basic', 'breakfast', 'cheesefare']
author: "italian boy"
---

## Ingredients

- 2 thermos, ½l capacity each
- thermometer
- 1l milk
- 100ml yogurt

## Directions

- bring the milk to 45°C (113°F)
- pour the yogurt into the milk
- wisk well
- bring the milk to 45°C (113°F) again (don't go higher than that, please)
- boil some water (about 100ml) and use it to wash the thermos from inside
- let the water out and pour the milk into the thermos
- leave the thermos in the oven(or in any other place whithout air flow) for 12h
- store in the fridge
>>>
